> single permutation. Since my knowledge of C never really made it past
> printf("hello world\n"); could someone please tell me which lines to put
> into include/config.h so that wizard mode works for my user account?

You're thinking of sh-style comments. These aren't commented out, rather
they're commands for the C preprocessor. Though not familiar with the
Nethack source I would say that things are fine, the only problem being
that you have to be the user 'wizard' before you can access Wizard mode.

You can change these "wizard" defines to your login name, compile again,
and then start Nethack with nethack -D. A quick ctrl-W will show whether
it worked or not.

